-- title:
--   Noetherian local ring with principal maximal ideal, generator non-nilpotent
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring that is Noetherian and local (in Mathlib's sense: it has a unique maximal ideal, denoted `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R`), and let $\tau \in R$. Assume that the maximal ideal of $R$ is the principal ideal generated by $\tau$, that is $\mathfrak{m}_R = (\tau)$, and that $\tau$ is not nilpotent, i.e. $\tau^n \neq 0$ for every natural number $n$ (note that this includes $n = 0$, so in particular $1 \neq 0$ and $R$ is nontrivial). The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions: $R$ is an integral domain, and $R$ is a principal ideal ring, i.e. every ideal of $R$ is generated by a single element. Equivalently, under these hypotheses $R$ is either a field (when $\tau$ is a unit, so $\mathfrak{m}_R = 0$) or a discrete valuation ring; the Lean statement records the two conclusions `IsDomain R` and `IsPrincipalIdealRing R` rather than this dichotomy.
--
--   This is the standard characterisation of discrete valuation rings among Noetherian local rings with principal maximal ideal, in the form that also allows the field case. It is used in the analysis of local charts, where it identifies the local ring of a blow-up chart at a point as a discrete valuation ring, via [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_algEquiv_coordRing_and_isDiscreteValuationRing_blowupChart_of_mem_maximalIdeal`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_algEquiv_coordRing_and_isDiscreteValuationRing_blowupChart_of_mem_maximalIdeal).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_isDomain_and_isPrincipalIdealRing_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_singleton.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
